sequenceDiagram
  participant Entry as updater / caller
  participant Source as source-sync
  participant Product as product public CLI
  participant Ledger as toolchain ledger
  participant Runner as schedule runner
  participant Scan as public diagnostics
  participant Queue as outbox / transport
  participant Fail as update-failure record
  Entry->>Source: normal run: root / main / origin / dirty guards
  Source->>Source: fetch + ancestor guard + ff-only
  Source-->>Entry: append source result and reopen Bash with result flag
  Note over Entry,Source: setup bypasses self-sync, log/restart failure is separate
  loop configured products
    Entry->>Product: compare / install / product-owned setup
    Product-->>Entry: exit and public result
    Entry->>Ledger: tracked CLIs only: operation with post gate pending
  end
  Entry->>Runner: post-update
  Runner->>Scan: capture report + ACK metadata once
  Scan-->>Runner: report ID + output path
  Runner->>Queue: flush earlier queue if reporting enabled
  Runner-->>Entry: process status / post gate result
  Note over Runner,Scan: scan completion is not every product check passing
  Entry->>Ledger: final post gate result for three CLIs
  alt final ledger writes and report ID available
    Entry->>Runner: finalize-update / expected report ID
    Runner->>Ledger: read final records
    Runner->>Runner: reproject last_update on same report
    Runner->>Queue: enqueue final bytes + existing ACK metadata
    Queue-->>Runner: flush exit status
    Runner->>Runner: write delivery receipt if reporting enabled
    Runner-->>Entry: finalized or explicit failure
  else final record / report ID missing
    Entry->>Entry: keep report failure, do not finalize
  end
  Entry->>Fail: record ran/failed steps and optional report evidence
  Fail-->>Entry: record / reporting outcome, failure only warns updater
  Entry-->>Entry: return update/report status
